rars-cli: no `AtomicU64` in the extraction staging counter (32-bit targets)

`crates/rars-cli/src/output.rs` names the private extraction directory
`.rars-extract-<pid>-<seq>` with a `static NEXT: AtomicU64`. 32-bit PowerPC,
MIPS and older ARM have no 64-bit atomics (`std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64`
does not exist there; the library crate already carries `atomic64.rs` for the
same reason, but it is `pub(crate)`). The sequence number only has to differ
between attempts within one process, so `AtomicUsize` is enough; `{:016x}`
keeps the zero-padded 16-digit name on every target.

--- crates/rars-cli/src/output.rs
+++ crates/rars-cli/src/output.rs
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 use std::collections::HashMap;
 use std::fs::{self, File, OpenOptions};
 use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
-use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};
+use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
 use std::time::SystemTime;
 
 /// Private, same-filesystem storage for a verified extraction's pending outputs.
@@ -17,7 +17,9 @@
 
